# Copy to infra/.env (gitignored); docker compose reads it automatically.
#
# Required for any deployment other machines can reach. Set it BEFORE the
# first `docker compose up`: Postgres bakes the password into the data
# volume on initialization. Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me

# REQUIRED. Compose refuses to start without it.
#
# One secret keys three things: Better Auth session signing, the GitHub
# install-cookie HMAC, and AES-256-GCM encryption of secrets at rest (the
# GitHub App private key and webhook secret). Minimum 32 characters; the app
# refuses anything shorter rather than deriving a weak key.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Treat rotation as a migration, not a config edit. Changing it signs everyone
# out, AND makes any GitHub App credentials encrypted under the old key
# undecryptable, so the GitHub integration has to be set up again. Rotate on
# suspected compromise or staff offboarding, with that cost understood.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Public origin of this deployment (scheme + host, no trailing slash). Used
# for OAuth callbacks and webhook URLs; required to be HTTPS when serving
# beyond localhost.
# APP_URL=https://specboards.example.com

# A database is REQUIRED for any deployment. Specboards refuses to start
# without DATABASE_URL rather than falling back to its local file store: that
# store has no accounts and no membership checks, so every request would be
# authorized, including deleting spec files. The compose stack sets
# DATABASE_URL for you from POSTGRES_PASSWORD above.
#
# SPECBOARDS_LOCAL_MODE=1 opts into that unauthenticated file store on purpose.
# It is for a single developer reading specs off a working tree, it is refused
# unless the server binds loopback and serves a localhost origin, and it must
# never be set on anything other people can reach. `pnpm dev` enables it
# automatically; you should not need it here.
